 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 11420,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2008\" data-start=\"1821\">Sympy can simplify and perform algebraic operations precisely.<br data-end=\"3524\" data-start=\"3521\" />\nExample:</p>\n\n<p>from sympy import simplify, symbols</p>\n\n<p>x = symbols(&#39;x&#39;)<br />\nexpr = (x**2 - 1)/(x - 1)<br />\nsimplified_expr = simplify(expr)</p>\n\n<p>print(simplified_expr) &nbsp;# x + 1</p>\n\n<p>For polynomial multiplication:</p>\n\n<p>from sympy import expand<br />\nexpr = (x + 2)*(x - 3)<br />\nresult = expand(expr)</p>\n\n<p>print(result) &nbsp;# x**2 - x - 6<br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"3985\" data-start=\"3841\">These show how symbolic algebra preserves the exactness of expression manipulation, useful in engineering, cryptography, and optimization tasks.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
